implemented against OpenSlope's portable map contracts and Trailmap's behavioral
specification. Its dependency list is recorded in ThirdPartyNotices/README.md.

The embedded shared contracts, ../Contracts/ride-v1.json and
../Contracts/external-sound-banks-v1.json, carry the bounded tuning facts and
functional identifiers described in ../Contracts/NOTICE. They supply
interoperability data, not original executable code, characters, media, or retail
assets.

Beyond those contracts, a bounded class of retail-derived facts appears in the
source itself: format and asset identifiers, disc and archive member names,
enumeration and bank names, the per-course lap counts and showoff clock lengths in
src/course_run.cpp (the values Slopesmith's src/core/doc/race.ts also carries),
and individual measured engine constants, each cited to the Trailmap chapter that
establishes it. Tests that run only against a user's local Maps folder assert
individual per-course measurements, such as record values, instance indices and
model or placement counts, as the evidence a behaviour was checked against. They
carry expected values, never the data, and the default test registration does not
run them. No retail instruction, asset, or executable accompanies any of this.
Native recreates neither the retail cast nor the retail trick repertoire.

No disc image, extracted game content, or game executable is distributed. Local map
loading consumes content supplied by the user; generated retail-derived content
remains local and excluded from releases. Disc import, including decoding course
audio and music from a user-supplied image, writes only to a Maps folder the user
chooses or to application-specific storage, and nothing it produces is packaged
into the application. Rights in the music and voice performances on a retail disc
are held by their publishers, labels, and performers; no grant here reaches them.
